  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "If the radius of earth shrinks by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>%</mo></math> while its mass remains same. The acceleration due to gravity on the earth&#39;s surface will approximately",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wWqRc",
      "text": "decrease by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>%</mo></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "h9mb8",
      "text": "decrease by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>%</mo></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "z5IH3",
      "text": "increase by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>%</mo></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "laZQy",
      "text": "increase by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>%</mo></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The acceleration due to gravity on the surface of the earth is given by,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>.</p><p>The radius shrunk by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>%</mo></math>. Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>%</mo></math>.</p><p>As the mass is constant and the change in the radius of the earth is relatively small, we can write</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>g</mi></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>g</mi></mstyle></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p><p>Hence, the acceleration due to gravity increases by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>%</mo></math>.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
